# Trivy temporary exceptions.
#
# Every entry must have a justification, an owner and a review date. Entries
# without those are not acceptable. CI still reports these findings in the
# SARIF/table output; they are only excluded from the *blocking* gate.
#
# Reviewed: 2026-11-08
# Review again: 2027-02-08

# CVE-2025-68121 (CRITICAL) — Go stdlib crypto/tls in /usr/local/bin/gosu,
# shipped by the official postgres:18.6-alpine image.
# gosu is a ~10 KB privilege-drop helper: it calls setgroups/setgid/setuid and
# execve, then exits. It never uses crypto/tls, net/http, net/url or crypto/x509,
# so this CVE is not reachable through the postgres container.
# Remove once the upstream postgres image rebuilds gosu with a patched Go
# toolchain (tracked upstream; the image itself is current for PostgreSQL 18.x).
CVE-2025-68121
